You know it's a bad day when...
I started the game with you wizard with strength 14, dexterity 18 (can't
remember other stats), a wand of lightning, a ring of regeneration and a ring
of conflict. On level 2 find a general store... Hmmm... try out the wand of
lightning, 3 zaps, shopkeeper's dead. Oh goody... 2 tins of spinach! Strength
of 16 now :-) Continue downwards, lots of monsters, reach exp level 7 by the
time I reach dlevel 6.. as I reach the bottom of the stair... WoW... bonus!
I remember this level.. I died here while attacking a shop keeper... at the 
time I was wearing a blessed gray dragon scale mail! Wander round the level
for a while, killing nasties, taming my old cat... into the shop... pick up
a lamp, rub it... MAGIC LAMP!!! get a my wish... a blessed +3 war hammer
named Mjollnir.. go to get the ghost.. kill the ghost, grab the GDSC, hey, 
it wasn't even cursed! By this time I have AC -13, 7 wands of various types,
many rings, intrinsics: speed, teleport, poison resistance, cold resistance,
fire resistance, telepathy... could have forgotten something here...
Also had almost every tool you could possibly need... no flute, harp or
bugle, but everything else... put on my blindfold to look for nasties... no
nasties on the level... oh dear... cursed blindfold! So I head back to a
fountain, not having any water potions, and hey presto! a water demon is
greatful for his release! Ummm... what do I want now....? Gauntlets of
Power! So, wearing my blessed +3 GoP, I head for another fountain, uncurse
my blindfold, and continue downwards... hit dlevel 13 (I knew 13 was a bad
number!) and everything stops... oh f***!
Go to another machine, ping my machine... no worries... go back to my other
session, try ^Q and various other things... no response...
Back to the other machine... rup machine
machine.anon.oz.au	up 12 days, 11:41,	load average: 640.95, 610.03 455.33

Next thing you know, machine is rebooted...
Sympathetic sysop tries to find a backup copy of game, but there isn't one...
Another Darling the Wizard bites the dust... this without even a corpse to
dream about finding...

Felt like murdering the joker with 
	for(;;){fork();}
in his program. Yup, that is what killed my game...

*sigh*

Emma.

